<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crossing of the Rubicon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The crossing of the Rubicon was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s decision in 49 BCE to lead his army across the Rubicon River in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the boundary of his province, in defiance of the Senate. The act began a civil war that ended with Caesar's dictatorship. It marked a decisive step in the transition from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crossing-of-the-rubicon.jpg" alt="Crossing of the Rubicon" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob Abbott · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crossing_the_Rubicon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
